              "text": "ನಟ (naṭa) is Sanskrit naṭa, \"dancer, actor\", taken over whole as a learned loan, a tatsama (CDIAL 6933). CDIAL 6933 thinks the Sanskrit word itself probably came from a Middle Indo-Aryan form. DEDR 2936 has a Kannada naṭike, \"the cracking of joints\", but that is a different word."
